comments.body:
I checked the current wiring. The right acpx primitive is `--model <id>` for the prompt run, and for an already-created named session `acpx <agent> set model <id> -s <name>` is explicitly routed to ACP `session/set_model`, not generic config. acpx docs call out that this is broader-compatible than `session/set_config_option`: https://github.com/openclaw/acpx/blob/main/docs/CLI.md#L333-L334 and https://github.com/openclaw/acpx/blob/main/docs/CLI.md#L455-L464.

Current Sepo shape:

- Provider selection already exists, but only at provider level: `AGENT_DEFAULT_PROVIDER` supports `auto`, `codex`, `claude` and auto prefers Codex when both secrets exist: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.github/actions/resolve-agent-provider/resolve-provider.sh#L68-L79
- The router passes that provider into `run-agent-task`: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.github/workflows/agent-router.yml#L360-L403
- `run-agent-task` exposes `agent` and `reasoning_effort`, but no model input yet: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.github/actions/run-agent-task/action.yml#L20-L31
- `run.ts` passes `MODEL_REASONING_EFFORT` into `runAcpx`, but no model: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.agent/src/run.ts#L547-L560
- `buildAcpxArgs` is the central place to add global acpx flags before the agent token, which is exactly where `--model` belongs: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.agent/src/acpx-adapter.ts#L223-L250
- The adapter already has session setup hooks for `set` and `set-mode`: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.agent/src/acpx-adapter.ts#L277-L315
- acpx model is already visible in raw session metadata and Sepo captures it in compact logs, but Sepo does not expose it as a first-class output/comment detail: https://github.com/self-evolving/repo/blob/main/.agent/src/acpx-adapter.ts#L518-L527

Recommended design: add one JSON repo variable, e.g. `AGENT_MODEL_POLICY`, rather than a pile of separate vars. Keep `AGENT_DEFAULT_PROVIDER` working as a backward-compatible provider-only shortcut.

Example shape:

```json
{
  "default": {
    "provider": "auto",
    "model": null,
    "reasoning_effort": "xhigh"
  },
  "providers": {
    "codex": {
      "model": "example-codex-model",
      "reasoning_effort": "xhigh"
    },
    "claude": {
      "model": "example-anthropic-model",
      "reasoning_effort": "max"
    }
  },
  "route_overrides": {
    "answer": {
      "provider": "codex",
      "model": "example-fast-codex-model"
    },
    "implement": {
      "provider": "codex"
    },
    "fix-pr": {
      "provider": "claude"
    },
    "review": {
      "lanes": [
        { "provider": "claude", "model": "example-anthropic-model", "reasoning_effort": "max" },
        { "provider": "codex", "model": "example-codex-model", "reasoning_effort": "xhigh" }
      ]
    },
    "review-synthesis": {
      "provider": "auto"
    }
  },
  "display": {
    "enabled": false
  }
}
```

Implementation plan I’d propose:

1. Add `.agent/src/model-policy.ts` with parser/validator/resolver, mirroring existing JSON policy patterns like memory/rubrics/schedule policies.
2. Extend `resolve-agent-provider` or add a sibling `resolve-agent-model` action so each route gets `{provider, model, reasoning_effort, display}` from `AGENT_MODEL_POLICY`, while preserving `AGENT_DEFAULT_PROVIDER`.
3. Add `model` and `display_model` inputs/outputs to `.github/actions/run-agent-task/action.yml`.
4. Thread `MODEL_ID` into `.agent/src/run.ts`, add `model?: string` to `AcpxRunOptions`, and push `--model <id>` in `buildAcpxArgs` before the agent token.
5. For persistent sessions, either rely on `--model` during prompt/reconnect or explicitly add `set model` in session setup. I’d start with `--model` because it is the documented global flag and acpx handles ACP model support/failure clearly.
6. Surface actual resolved model/provider as outputs. Best source is the compact session entry when available; fallback to the configured requested model.
7. If `display.enabled` or a simpler `AGENT_DISPLAY_MODEL=true` is set, append a short footer to posted Sepo comments, e.g. `Run: codex / <model> / xhigh`.
8. Update docs in `.agent/docs/customization/configuration-list.md` and tests around provider resolution, acpx args, workflow envelope snapshots, and comment/display formatting.

One clarification before coding: should the display flag show only the model, or provider + model + reasoning effort? I’d recommend provider + model + reasoning effort because model IDs alone can be ambiguous across Codex/Anthropic adapters.
